    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 score makes him our primary offensive engine. He benefits from a prime matchup against Curry, whose 5.68 xERA suggests significant vulnerability. The +19% bump from the favorable pitching matchup, combined with his placement in the three-hole, makes **Gunnar Henderson** a must-start in all formats. Supporting him are **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.07) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.71), both of whom are projected for strong performances. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically earns a nod due to a 14% boost from a favorable platoon matchup, while **Jackson Merrill** (71.39) stands out as an elite play; despite a moderate matchup, his 14% park-factor adjustment highlights his capacity to capitalize on today\u2019s environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Tommy White**, who produced a 48.09 score, narrowly missing the cut behind the marginal start of **Wade Meckler** (51.82). While **Tommy White** posted respectable metrics, he suffered from a negative park-factor adjustment and a lower lineup position compared to **Wade Meckler**, who secured a higher score due to a superior platoon advantage. On the risk front, **Nasim Nunez** warrants caution; although his elite speed remains a vital asset for our SB-starved roster, his 41.02 score sits dangerously close to our floor of 40.0. Facing a high-caliber arm in Wheeler, combined with a bottom-of-the-order assignment, makes **Nasim Nunez** a player to watch closely as he navigates a tough individual matchup. We remain without **Andy Pages**, who continues to sit on the IL, leaving our current outfield rotation to lean heavily on the consistency of **Kyle Tucker** and the utility depth provided by **Josh Jung** and **Coby Mayo**.",
